The [org.apache.juneau.commons.concurrent](pathname:///site/apidocs/org/apache/juneau/commons/concurrent/package-summary.html) package provides small concurrency helpers that make locks and atomic references work cleanly with try-with-resources and `Optional`-style APIs.

## Auto-Closeable Locks

### <java-class><a href="/site/apidocs/org/apache/juneau/commons/concurrent/SimpleLock.html" target="_blank">SimpleLock</a></java-class>
An `AutoCloseable` wrapper around a `java.util.concurrent.locks.Lock` that acquires the lock on construction and releases it on `close()`, so it can be used directly in a try-with-resources block. The `SimpleLock.NO_OP` constant is a do-nothing lock.

```java
try (SimpleLock ignored = new SimpleLock(myLock)) {
    // critical section — lock released automatically
}
```

### <java-class><a href="/site/apidocs/org/apache/juneau/commons/concurrent/SimpleReadWriteLock.html" target="_blank">SimpleReadWriteLock</a></java-class>
An extension of `ReentrantReadWriteLock` whose `read()` and `write()` methods return auto-closeable `SimpleLock` instances. `SimpleReadWriteLock.NO_OP` is a do-nothing variant.

```java
SimpleReadWriteLock rw = new SimpleReadWriteLock();

try (SimpleLock ignored = rw.read()) {
    // read-locked section
}
try (SimpleLock ignored = rw.write()) {
    // write-locked section
}
```

## Atomic References

### <java-class><a href="/site/apidocs/org/apache/juneau/commons/concurrent/NullableReference.html" target="_blank">NullableReference</a></java-class>
A thread-safe reference that combines `AtomicReference` with `Optional`-like convenience methods (`isPresent()`, `map()`, `flatMap()`, `filter()`, `of()`/`ofNullable()`/`empty()`).

```java
NullableReference<String> ref = NullableReference.of("hello");
boolean present = ref.isPresent();
NullableReference<Integer> len = ref.map(String::length);
```

