The <a href="/site/apidocs/org/apache/juneau/marshall/uon/UonSerializer.html" target="_blank">UonSerializer</a> class is used to serialize POJOs into UON.

## When to use it

Use `UonSerializer` for values that travel in URLs or HTTP headers, where JSON's braces, quotes and colons would need escaping.
UON writes a bean as `(name=value,...)` and a collection as `@(a,b)`, so the result drops into a query-string or header value with little extra encoding.
For a whole `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` body, use [URL-Encoding](/docs/topics/UrlEncodingSupport), which builds on UON.

## Example

```java
import org.apache.juneau.marshall.uon.*;

public class UonSerializerExample {

    public static class Person {
        public String name = "John Smith";
        public int age = 45;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        Person person = new Person();

        // Compact, single-line output.
        System.out.println(UonSerializer.DEFAULT.write(person));

        // Same data, indented for reading.
        System.out.println(UonSerializer.DEFAULT_READABLE.write(person));
    }
}
```

The compact form is `(age=45,name='John Smith')`. Properties are written in alphabetical order.

## Options

The following pre-configured serializers are provided for convenience:

| Instance | Output |
|---|---|
| `UonSerializer.DEFAULT` | Compact output; strings are quoted only when they need to be. |
| `UonSerializer.DEFAULT_READABLE` | Indented, multi-line output for people. |
| `UonSerializer.DEFAULT_ENCODING` | URL-encodes characters that are unsafe in a URL. |

For anything else, start from the builder's `create()` method. The settings readers reach for first:

| Builder method | Effect |
|---|---|
| `encoding()` | URL-encode unsafe characters in the output. |
| `paramFormat(...)` / `paramFormatPlain()` | Control how top-level values are written when used as URL parameters. |
| `addBeanTypesUon()` | Add `_type` properties to beans whose runtim...

The <a href="/site/apidocs/org/apache/juneau/marshall/uon/UonParser.html" target="_blank">UonParser</a> class is used to parse UON into POJOs.

## When to use it

Use `UonParser` to read UON text, such as a header value or a URL parameter that [UonSerializer](/docs/topics/UonSerializers) wrote, back into POJOs.
If the text arrives URL-encoded (`%20` for a space), use the decoding instance so the escapes are resolved first.

## Example

```java
import org.apache.juneau.marshall.uon.*;

public class UonParserExample {

    public static class Person {
        public String name;
        public int age;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // Plain UON.
        Person a = UonParser.DEFAULT.read("(name='John Smith',age=45)", Person.class);

        // UON whose characters are URL-encoded.
        Person b = UonParser.DEFAULT_DECODING.read("(name='John%20Smith',age=45)", Person.class);

        System.out.println(a.name + " " + a.age + ", " + b.name + " " + b.age);
    }
}
```



## Options

The following pre-configured parsers are provided for convenience:

| Instance | Accepts |
|---|---|
| `UonParser.DEFAULT` | Plain UON text. |
| `UonParser.DEFAULT_DECODING` | UON text with URL-encoded characters, decoded before parsing. |

For anything else, start from the builder's `create()` method. The settings readers reach for first:

| Builder method | Effect |
|---|---|
| `decoding()` | URL-decode the input before parsing. |
| `validateEnd()` | Fail if anything but whitespace follows the parsed value. |
| `trimStrings()` | Trim whitespace from parsed string values. |
| `autoCloseStreams()` | Close the input stream or reader when parsing finishes. |
| `beanDictionary(Class...)` | Classes the parser may instantiate from `_type` properties. |
| `swaps(Class...)` | Object swaps that convert parsed values into other types. |

